WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.720
Today's Today's Blend is another hit!

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.600
That's good to hear.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.690
Guatemala and Mandheling and Brazil...

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.260
And a lightly roasted Mocha?

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.500
You got it!

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.820
Some people say that you're not a 
connoisseur if you put milk or sugar in,

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.790
but that's plain wrong.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:18.750
You're amazing.

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:21.820
I'm not good at accepting compliments.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.260
Looks like it'll take a while to fill that spot.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:33.080
She hasn't brought it up lately, 
so we don't want to ask, either.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.970
She's not worrying herself again, is she?

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:40.530
Because I did jokingly say that that would 
be the corner for Himeno's best pieces.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.170
I don't get the feeling  
she's worrying at all.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.030
She's been making piece after 
piece for the cultural festival

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.300
and keeping on top of the preparations 
with the class as well.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.970
That's good, I guess.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:54.950
However...

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:59.950
It's not like there isn't something 
that doesn't not feel off.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.190
Huh? What do you mean?

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.590
Well, I'm still observing.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.460
<b>Ori Aca Cultural Festival</b>

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.460
<i>Not knowing that they 
were talking like that,</i>

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.900
<i>all of a sudden the actual 
Cultural Festival was here.</i>

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.470
<b>House of Terror</b>

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.990
Ori Aca 
Cultural
 Festival

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.670
That will be 150 Yen.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.860
Thank you very much.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:26.590
People from all the other schools are here.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:29.760
We've got students from Tajimi Tech, and 
Tajimi High, North High and West High!

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.800
Of course! It's a festival, after all!

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.370
Looks like business is booming.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.890
Sensei!

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.380
Thanks to you.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.280
Isn't it almost time for the three 
of you to go back to your classrooms?

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.380
I'll take over.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.060
We're sorry that we all have
 to leave at the same time.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.630
Thank you for covering for us.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.610
<i>I wasn't planning on worrying.</i>

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.760
<i>Not yet.</i>

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:26.390
<b>Supersized ♥ Cultural Festival</b>

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:27.230
Our delicious coffee and cheese 
tarts are almost sold out!

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.700
Do step in!

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:32.310
Is there room for three, miss?

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.390
Touko-senpai?!

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:42.980
What's that outfit?!

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.650
It's my class' project, and I was forced...

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:47.750
She looks so cool though, doesn't she?

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.870
Like she'll just sweep me off my feet.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.590
Right?

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:54.990
Wait, we met you two back in the contest!

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.200
We're Noa and Yuzuna!

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.260
We bought bowls from the pottery club.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.480
Wow, really?

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.700
Thank you so much!

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.970
Come on in.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.000
Seating a party of three!

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:10.590
Be tasty... Be tasty....

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.160
Be tasty... Be tasty....

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.370
I don't think you need to do that.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.660
In fact, it's probably better if you don't.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.020
Really?

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:24.930
Nao-chan said this was a 
fool-proof way of doing it.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.770
Sounds like something she'd say...

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.750
This is so good!

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.570
It's the best.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:34.920
Your mom's mugs are amazing, too!

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.570
Thank you!

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:41.320
It feels so good in my hand and 
the coloring is just genius.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.070
You're right.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.800
The color is so translucent and wondrous.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:50.140
It's not a color you can achieve quickly.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.540
Thank you so much!

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.540
I bet my mom is happy to hear that, too!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.400
Yes. She's probably saying, 
"I've finally finished."

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.110
Huh?

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:00.930
Dad?

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:02.270
Kusano-sensei?

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:04.570
That outfit looks good on you, Aoki-san.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.790
Please don't say that...

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.320
It really does!

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:12.100
I wanted to enjoy the parent-child collab.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.040
And I came with him to surprise you.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.020
You should've told me!

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:19.600
But what did you mean by 
"I've finally finished"?

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:28.410
She often said that a piece wasn't 
done when it'd been fired.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.850
A piece was only done once 
it had made someone happy.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.170
So deep!

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:41.170
<i>Once it has made someone happy...</i>

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.780
<b>Piece for the contest</b>

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:44.190
By Aoki Touko

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:48.240
<b>New piece for the Ori Aca Festival</b>

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.920
You did a great job, Aoki-san.

00:05:58.130 --> 00:05:59.450
Welcome!

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.910
You're Aoki-san's...

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.060
Yeah, it's good.

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.290
72 points.

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.740
What? That's awkward.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:24.020
I give this collaboration 
with your mother 100 points.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.940
Thank you!

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.570
This reminds me of old times.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:32.070
I guess they aren't using blackboards anymore.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.290
White boards and tablets are the norm now.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.680
Seriously?

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.790
It's shocking when you come 
back after so long, huh?

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.790
They also changed the pool into a gym.

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.870
The main building has been renovated, too.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:46.330
But do you know the only part that hasn't changed?

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:48.330
The pottery classroom.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.070
Thank you!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.370
Thank you, Sensei!

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.200
Welcome back!

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.440
We've sold quite a lot of 
the bowls and whatnot.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:03.860
I'll change and take over for you.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.570
A-Aoki-san!

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:08.850
Look... at you!

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.970
Oh, this...

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:16.160
Uhm... could I... take a picture?

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.660
I guess that would be okay.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:22.120
I'm terribly sorry, but could you....

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.840
All right, here I go!

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:27.630
Say cheese!

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:33.250
Thank you so much!

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:36.530
But more importantly...

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:39.220
Have you applied for for your 
grandfather's special exhibit?

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.440
No, I'm not going to.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.040
What?!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.180
Wh... Wh-Why not?

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:50.880
I did it before because I had lost my confidence, 
but that's not the case anymore.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.790
Now all I have to say is this.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.790
You... made this?

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.690
Yes.

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:14.840
When I completely emptied my mind,
 this is how it turned out.

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:18.720
<i>The delicate glow of the red glaze...</i>

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.190
<i>The powerful gold glaze.</i>

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:26.240
<i>So different than anything 
she's made before.</i>

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.180
What a wonderful day this is!

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:38.380
I'm going to make something even 
better than this, so just you wait!

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.780
Uh, sure.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.780
I won't let you beat me!

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:46.600
Okay!

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.540
She's a bit of a strange girl.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:53.260
Yes. But she's become a valuable friend.

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.010
Oh, so...

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.480
Did my grandfather come?

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:02.450
Oh, well...

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.570
Of course. He didn't...

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:09.330
Wow, this hasn't changed one bit!

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.750
Toyokawa-senpai. Kusano-senpai!

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:17.190
This takes me back.

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.160
They've even got that old fan!

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:22.580
Wait, they have AC now?

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:25.220
Chill out, dad.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:27.650
Oh, sorry.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:28.590
That reminds me.

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:30.680
I wonder if they still have it...

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:31.570
"It"?

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.840
Oh, that.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.970
<b>Haunted House</b>

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:38.970
<b>Entrance</b>

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.410
I'm so tired!

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:53.610
I need Hime-chan to replenish my tired body.

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.220
Just a little bit longer, Naruse-san!

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:56.220
Huh?

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:59.120
Your ghost is the most popular!

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:03.990
Please, no!

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:07.950
Now where was it?

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:12.990
Is one of mom's masterpieces 
really hidden here?

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:15.490
We've cleaned up so many 
times, so if it were here,

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:18.220
I'm sure we would've noticed it.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.270
It didn't get thrown away, right, Senpai?

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:24.510
Of course not. Not something that good.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:26.510
Now I really want to see it!

00:10:26.510 --> 00:10:28.210
It must be amazing!

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:32.320
It was passed down from generation to 
generation, so it's got to be here somewhere.

00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:34.390
That reminds me...

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.620
The previous president

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:39.640
gave me something mysterious and told me 
to make sure it never got thrown away.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.160
That's it, that's it! That's the box.

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.800
It's still here!

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.400
This is exactly it.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:52.860
It's been so long since I've seen it.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:54.500
This is it?

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:58.040
I was wondering what that was doing here.

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:02.070
So the previous president didn't tell you
 why you can't throw it away, Touko-senpai?

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.730
That's right. It's been a mystery all this time.

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:06.380
It's interesting, huh?

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:09.070
This is Toyokawa Himena's failed piece.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:11.530
That's what it is!

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:14.220
So why did she bother to fire it?

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:18.060
I remember that time well...

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:23.630
Having won her first pottery 
contest at the age of ten,

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:26.850
by the first year of high school, 
she already had pro-level skills.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.780
You really are amazing, huh?

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:35.950
Well, if it's a normal bowl,
I could even do it with my feet.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:38.250
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.850
So there she was, spouting nonsense when...

00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:47.290
You've made a masterpiece, alright.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:51.570
It was the only time she messed up
 in all three years of high school.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:55.480
Actually, her first failure in eight years.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:56.430
I've decided.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:58.600
I'm going to put this in 
the kiln and fire it.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:11:59.620
What?

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.860
I really see now that one must stay humble.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:05.530
By putting this into a lasting form

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:09.560
it will serve as a caution that we must 
always treat the clay with respect!

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.450
Oh, I see!

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:15.870
So even the legendary
 Tokikawa Himena made mistakes.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:19.880
The way she messed up and the way
 she took it were both so like her.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.750
I never knew.

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.860
You just don't remember.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.660
But I'm glad the mystery's solved!

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:29.900
If you don't know the story, it just 
looks like some garbage piece.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.520
Totally!

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.400
Still...

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:42.130
I can't believe she actually 
fired it and passed it down.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.230
I mean, if you made as many mistakes as me,

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:49.280
you'd never, ever want 
to make them permanent.

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:58.430
<i>Mom really is a legend, huh?</i>

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:04.020
<i>That was the moment when the worry inside me,
 that I hadn't even realized was there,</i>

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:07.320
<i>grew slightly bigger again.</i>

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:28.120
When the bob-haired girl is once again 
having trouble with making progress,

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:35.310
<b>The Mini Mini Pottery Club</b>

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:30.780
a certain famous performer appears!

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:34.520
It's actually an acquaintance 
of Forehead's grandfather...

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.540
Next time, "Good Day For the Pottery Wheel".

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Good Day For the Pottery Wheel</b>

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:39.970
<b>Next time:</b>

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.610
But that also means we're getting closer.
